 209, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/68/en_b1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 61.55, "size_bytes": 370224, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 209, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/68/en_b1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/68/en_b1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 65.575, "size_bytes": 394416, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 209, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/68/en_b1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/68/en_b1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 56.5, "size_bytes": 339984, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 209, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/68/en_b1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/68/en_b1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 61.675, "size_bytes": 370944, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 209, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/68/en_b1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@db9d57c/content/data/versions/673.json", "paragraphs": ["On Thursday, the Cleveland Guardians beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series. Because of this win, the Guardians now lead the best-of-seven series 2-1. Game 4 is set for Friday, although rain is in the forecast.", "Petey Halpin hit a two-run home run in the fifth inning that put Cleveland ahead. It was his first playoff home run. Gavin Williams started the game and struck out nine batters over five innings, allowing two runs. He has been strong all postseason.", "The Cleveland bullpen also did well. They retired 16 of the Rays' final 17 batters. Cade Smith struck out Yandy Díaz in the eighth to leave a runner on third, and then he retired the side in order in the ninth. Tampa Bay struck out 13 times in the game.", "José Ramírez had two hits for Cleveland, and Nathaniel Lowe added an RBI double in the second inning. Chandler Simpson hit a two-run triple in the fourth to give the Rays a short lead, but Halpin's home run decided the game."], "paragraphs_zh": ["周四，克利夫兰守护者队在美联冠军系列赛第三场中以3-2击败坦帕湾光芒队。因为这场胜利，守护者队现在在七场四胜制的系列赛中以2-1领先。第四场比赛定于周五举行，不过天气预报有雨。", "皮特·哈尔平在第五局击出两分全垒打，让克利夫兰取得领先。这是他季后赛的第一个全垒打。加文·威廉姆斯先发主投五局，三振了九名打者，失掉两分。他在整个季后赛中表现一直很出色。", "克利夫兰的牛棚也表现出色。他们让光芒队最后17名打者中的16名出局。凯德·史密斯在第八局三振了扬迪·迪亚兹，留下一名跑者在三垒，然后他在第九局让对手三上三下。坦帕湾在这场比赛中被三振13次。", "何塞·拉米雷斯为克利夫兰贡献了两支安打，纳撒尼尔·洛在第二局添上一支带有一分打点的二垒安打。钱德勒·辛普森在第四局击出两分三垒安打，让光芒队短暂领先，但哈尔平的全垒打决定了比赛。"], "body": "On Thursday, the Cleveland Guardians beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series. Because of this win, the Guardians now lead the best-of-seven series 2-1. Game 4 is set for Friday, although rain is in the forecast.\n\nPetey Halpin hit a two-run home run in the fifth inning that put Cleveland ahead. It was his first playoff home run. Gavin Williams started the game and struck out nine batters over five innings, allowing two runs. He has been strong all postseason.\n\nThe Cleveland bullpen also did well. They retired 16 of the Rays' final 17 batters. Cade Smith struck out Yandy Díaz in the eighth to leave a runner on third, and then he retired the side in order in the ninth. Tampa Bay struck out 13 times in the game.\n\nJosé Ramírez had two hits for Cleveland, and Nathaniel Lowe added an RBI double in the second inning. Chandler Simpson hit a two-run triple in the fourth to give the Rays a short lead, but Halpin's home run decided the game.", "body_zh": "周四，克利夫兰守护者队在美联冠军系列赛第三场中以3-2击败坦帕湾光芒队。因为这场胜利，守护者队现在在七场四胜制的系列赛中以2-1领先。第四场比赛定于周五举行，不过天气预报有雨。\n\n皮特·哈尔平在第五局击出两分全垒打，让克利夫兰取得领先。这是他季后赛的第一个全垒打。加文·威廉姆斯先发主投五局，三振了九名打者，失掉两分。他在整个季后赛中表现一直很出色。\n\n克利夫兰的牛棚也表现出色。他们让光芒队最后17名打者中的16名出局。凯德·史密斯在第八局三振了扬迪·迪亚兹，留下一名跑者在三垒，然后他在第九局让对手三上三下。坦帕湾在这场比赛中被三振13次。\n\n何塞·拉米雷斯为克利夫兰贡献了两支安打，纳撒尼尔·洛在第二局添上一支带有一分打点的二垒安打。钱德勒·辛普森在第四局击出两分三垒安打，让光芒队短暂领先，但哈尔平的全垒打决定了比赛。", "text": "On Thursday, the Cleveland Guardians beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series. Because of this win, the Guardians now lead the best-of-seven series 2-1. Game 4 is set for Friday, although rain is in the forecast. Petey Halpin hit a two-run home run in the fifth inning that put Cleveland ahead. It was his first playoff home run. Gavin Williams started the game and struck out nine batters over five innings, allowing two runs. He has been strong all postseason. The Cleveland bullpen also did well. They retired 16 of the Rays' final 17 batters. Cade Smith struck out Yandy Díaz in the eighth to leave a runner on third, and then he retired the side in order in the ninth. Tampa Bay struck out 13 times in the game. José Ramírez had two hits for Cleveland, and Nathaniel Lowe added an RBI double in the second inning. Chandler Simpson hit a two-run triple in the fourth to give the Rays a short lead, but Halpin's home run decided the game.", "vocab": [{"word": "home run", "pos": "noun", "zh": "全垒打", "note": "棒球术语，指击球手将球击出外野围墙，通常可得1-4分。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "strike out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "三振出局", "note": "动词短语，指投手让击球手挥棒落空三次出局。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "bullpen", "pos": "noun", "zh": "牛棚（替补投手群）", "note": "指球队的替补投手，也指他们热身的地方。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "retire", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使出局", "note": "在棒球中，指让打者出局。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inning", "pos": "noun", "zh": "局", "note": "棒球比赛的单位，一场比赛通常有九局。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "RBI", "pos": "noun", "zh": "打点（带打点安打）", "note": "Run Batted In 的缩写，指击球手击球让队友得分。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "postseason", "pos": "noun", "zh": "季后赛", "note": "指常规赛之后进行的比赛。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "series", "pos": "noun", "zh": "系列赛", "note": "指两支球队之间进行的多场比赛。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lead", "pos": "noun", "zh": "领先", "note": "指在比赛中处于优势地位。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "forecast", "pos": "noun", "zh": "预报", "note": "常指天气预报。", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Petey Halpin’s two-run homer lifts Guardians past Rays for 2-1 ALCS lead", "summary_original": "Halpin’s first playoff homer puts Cleveland ahead\nWilliams strikes out nine as Guardians win 3-2\nCleveland bullpen retires 11 of final 12 Rays batters\nPetey Halpin hit a go-ahead two-run homer, Gavin Williams struck out nine over five innings and the Cleveland Guardians beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series on Thursday to take a 2-1 lead.\nGame 4 of the best-of-seven series is scheduled for Friday, though rain is forecast.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Petey Halpin’s two-run homer lifts Guardians past Rays for 2-1 ALCS lead\nHalpin’s first playoff homer puts Cleveland ahead\nWilliams strikes out nine as Guardians win 3-2\nCleveland bullpen retires 11 of final 12 Rays batters\nPetey Halpin hit a go-ahead two-run homer, Gavin Williams struck out nine over five innings and the\nCleveland Guardians\nbeat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series on Thursday to take a 2-1 lead.\nGame 4 of the best-of-seven series is scheduled for Friday, though rain is forecast.\nJosé Ramírez had two hits and Nathaniel Lowe added an RBI for the Guardians, who have won five of their last six playoff games since falling 2-0 behind the Chicago White Sox in their AL Division Series.\nWilliams allowed two runs over five innings while walking one. He is 2-0 with a 2.16 ERA and 33 strikeouts over 16 and two-thirds innings innings in four postseason appearances this year, including three starts.\nCleveland retired 16 of the Rays’ final 17 batters. Daniel Espino, Erik Sabrowski, Hunter Gaddis and Cade Smith combined to allow just one baserunner over the final four innings.\nSmith stranded a runner at third in the eighth when he struck out Yandy Díaz after a 10-pitch at-bat, then retired the side in order in the ninth.\nTampa Bay went down in order in seven innings, with Junior Caminero striking out four times. Rays batters struck out 13 times in Game 3 after combining for 14 in the first two games of the series.\nLowe opened the scoring with an RBI double in the second that bounced off the right-field fence and past Victor Mesa Jr.\nChandler Simpson put the Rays ahead with a two-run triple in the fourth.\nPatrick Bailey led off the fifth with a chopper that pitcher Griffin Jax was unable to field cleanly. Halpin then connected on an elevated 95.9mph sinker on a 2-2 count, driving it 385ft into the right-center-field stands to give Cleveland a 3-2 lead.\nIt was Halpin’s first postseason home run and only the fifth of his two-year major league career. Jax had not allowed a homer since 9 September, a span of five appearances.\nWilliams did not allow a baserunner and struck out five the first time through the order.\nJax allowed three runs on five hits and two walks in four-plus innings.\nExplore more on these topics\nMLB\nCleveland Guardians\nTampa Bay Rays\nBaseball\nUS sports\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-15T23:47:20.173050", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "On", "s": 0.25, "e": 0.425, "sm": 250, "em": 425, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Thursday", "s": 0.425, "e": 1.025, "sm": 425, "em": 1024, "cs": 3, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.1, "sm": 1025, "em": 1099, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "the", "s": 1.1, "e": 1.2, "sm": 1100, "em": 1199, "cs": 13, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "Cleveland", "s": 1.2, "e": 1.625, "sm": 1200, "em": 1625, "cs": 17, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Guardians", "s": 1.625, "e": 2.15, "sm": 1625, "em": 2149, "cs": 27, "ce": 36, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "beat", "s": 2.15, "e": 2.337, 